pe\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Clarifying diagnosis urgency**\\n\\nI need to ensure I provide a complete and updated diagnosis without additional questions. It's important to mention the need for urgent escalation, especially since the symptoms were ambiguous and not clearly specified. I'll advise the user to go to the emergency room if any of those symptoms are present. If appropriate, I might suggest using our kidney pipeline tool and invite them to upload the CT image for further evaluation.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Clinical picture**\nYou have a **progressively worsening constant right-sided back/flank pain**, **visible pink to red urine**, **some fever**, severe **exhaustion**, and **major unintended weight loss (28 kg in 3 months)**. From your structured record, there is also **renal cell carcinoma follow-up after nephrectomy**, prior **mild hematuria**, **creatinine 1.4 mg/dL**, **eGFR 61**, and current **sunitinib** treatment. Taken together, this is **not reassuring** and needs urgent in-person evaluation.\n\n**Most likely possibilities**\n- **A kidney/urinary tract process that requires urgent reassessment**, including possible **tumor recurrence/progression or another structural renal problem**. This is strongly supported by the combination of **visible hematuria**, **one-sided persistent pain**, **weight loss**, **fever**, and your prior RCC history.\n- **Urinary tract obstruction, bleeding source, or infection involving the kidney/urinary tract**. Fever and hematuria can fit this, and these can become serious quickly.\n- **Treatment-related fatigue or systemic illness** may be contributing to the exhaustion and weight loss, but this would **not adequately explain away** the persistent one-sided pain and gross hematuria.\n- **Musculoskeletal back pain** is now **less supported** as the main explanation, because the urinary bleeding and systemic symptoms point much more toward a renal/urologic cause.\n\n**Confidence / uncertainty note**\nThere is a **high level of concern** that this is more than ordinary back pain or routine treatment fatigue. I cannot confirm the exact cause from chat alone, but the current pattern is sufficiently concerning that it should be treated as a **potentially serious kidney/urologic or oncologic issue** until proven otherwise. What needs clinician confirmation urgently is the source of the bleeding, the cause of the weight loss/fever, and whether there is recurrence, obstruction, infection, or another complication.\n\n**Red flags / urgent concerns**\nYour current symptoms contain **multiple red flags**:\n- **Visible blood in urine**\n- **Rapid major weight loss**\n- **Persistent worsening one-sided back/flank pain**\n- **Fever**\n- **Known RCC follow-up / post-nephrectomy history**\n\nBecause of this, I recommend **urgent same-day in-person assessment**. If you are currently having **difficulty urinating, very low urine output, severe weakness, dizziness, shortness of breath, chest pain, severe worsening pain, or feel acutely unwell**, go to the **emergency department now** rather than waiting for an outpatient appointment.\n\n**What to do next**\nPlease contact your **oncology/urology team immediately today**. The type of evaluation clinicians often consider in this situation may include:\n- **urinalysis and blood tests**\n- **kidney function testing**\n- **urgent imaging** of the kidneys/urinary tract/abdomen\n- assessment for **bleeding, infection, obstruction, or recurrence**\n\nGiven the kidney-focused concern here, if you have a **new CT scan image** available, you can also use the **kidney cancer detection pipeline** by uploading that CT image, and I can help summarize the result for you.  \nImportant: that tool would provide only a **preliminary signal**, **not an actual diagnosis**.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0d6bacbc4fba24af0169da6d3d47ec819189dd30ad04b944a6\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":936,"output":748,"cacheRead":13440,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15124,"cost":{"input":0.00234,"output":0.01122,"cacheRead":0.0033599999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.01692}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775922489154}}
{"type":"message","id":"a7313f6a","parentId":"79b458d9","timestamp":"2026-04-11T15:48:50.103Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[media attached: /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_3---c4f08b6f-67f7-4ba5-b143-433c0ce68cda.jpg (image/jpeg) | /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_3---c4f08b6f-67f7-4ba5-b143-433c0ce68cda.jpg]\nTo send an image back, prefer the message tool (media/path/filePath). If you must inline, use MEDIA:https://example.com/image.jpg (spaces ok, quote if needed) or a safe relative path like MEDIA:./image.jpg. Avoid absolute paths (MEDIA:/...) and ~ paths — they are blocked for security. Keep caption in the text body.\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"352\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"567556397\",\n  \"sender\": \"Andrea Pitrone\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sat 2026-04-11 15:48 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Andrea Pitrone (567556397)\",\n  \"id\": \"567556397\",\n  \"name\": \"Andrea Pitrone\",\n  \"username\": \"pitro_eng_guitarist\"\n}\n```\n\n<media:image>"},{"type":"image","data":"","mimeType":"image/jpeg"}],"timestamp":1775922530100}}
