nd family history of renal cell carcinoma. Red flags present: gross hematuria, progressive unilateral pain, fever, major weight loss, prior RCC history.\" --diagnosis \"Tool: kidney CT pipeline. Kidney Cancer Detector classification: kidney_tumor. Confidence: 0.9999004602432251 (~99.99%). Image Analyzer prediction: kidney_tumor. CAM metrics: coverage 0.03220663265306122, center_ratio 0.049504950490148025, lr_asym 0.5445544553916283, tb_asym 0.9999999999009902. CAM explanation: model focused on a localized peripheral renal region with asymmetric spatial distribution, suggesting a localized structural alteration. X-AI summary: image likely related to kidney cancer based on model prediction and confidence. Confidence interpretation: highly reliable prediction but must be considered with other diagnostic information and medical literature for comprehensive understanding. Recommended next steps from tool: further CT or MRI, biopsy/tissue sampling if appropriate, consultation with urologist or oncologist. Caveat: pipeline output is a preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\"","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent","yieldMs":15000,"timeout":120},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/llm-distillator/scripts/distill_health_response.py --context \\\"Patient reports progressive exhaustion and a persistent dull/constant right-sided lower back or flank pain that has been worsening over the last few months. Pain occurs with movement and also at rest. He reports visible pinkish to red urine, some fever, and severe unintentional weight loss of 28 kg over the last 3 months. Structured patient knowledge base shows recent fatigue, mild hematuria, creatinine 1.4 mg/dL, eGFR 61 mL/min/1.73m², RCC follow-up after nephrectomy, current sunitinib 50 mg daily, and family history of renal cell carcinoma. Red flags present: gross hematuria, progressive unilateral pain, fever, major weight loss, prior RCC history.\\\" --diagnosis \\\"Tool: kidney CT pipeline. Kidney Cancer Detector classification: kidney_tumor. Confidence: 0.9999004602432251 (~99.99%). Image Analyzer prediction: kidney_tumor. CAM metrics: coverage 0.03220663265306122, center_ratio 0.049504950490148025, lr_asym 0.5445544553916283, tb_asym 0.9999999999009902. CAM explanation: model focused on a localized peripheral renal region with asymmetric spatial distribution, suggesting a localized structural alteration. X-AI summary: image likely related to kidney cancer based on model prediction and confidence. Confidence interpretation: highly reliable prediction but must be considered with other diagnostic information and medical literature for comprehensive understanding. Recommended next steps from tool: further CT or MRI, biopsy/tissue sampling if appropriate, consultation with urologist or oncologist. Caveat: pipeline output is a preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-demo-agent\",\"yieldMs\":15000,\"timeout\":120}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":966,"output":433,"cacheRead":26496,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27895,"cost":{"input":0.002415,"output":0.006495,"cacheRead":0.006624,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.015534}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775922700775}}
