lY3Jx_Sf5u-r_lBszhUWQBop3HO12jSVzlTuOCacBecynmCMUTfsraSGRwTmPnVZHz1FiSy7EBxqNcOpDJTWRMwMBlGCuJ5DKo0AEUcV-L9CwmfZECs1RLdQx-iqyhtUqL2y2Z-lkwO7OwzhXY1X6JvN0s-lIvLLWMaDr27feWBB-w09TeQ==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Addressing tool unavailability**\\n\\nThe user needs to know that the tool isn’t available, but I can provide a manual distilled summary instead. I should mention that I checked, but it’s not related to memory. It might be good to ask if the user is satisfied with this approach. Since the distillation tool isn’t working, I’ll deliver the information in a distilled style and clarify that the dedicated tool is unavailable right now.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Distilled summary**\nYour current picture is **highly concerning for a serious kidney/urinary tract problem** rather than simple back pain. The combination of **constant right-sided back/flank pain, visible blood in the urine, fever, severe fatigue, and a 28 kg unintentional weight loss over 3 months**, together with your known **renal cell carcinoma follow-up history after nephrectomy**, means this needs **urgent specialist reassessment**.\n\n**What the imaging pipeline adds**\nThe kidney CT pipeline flagged the uploaded image as **kidney_tumor** with **very high confidence**, and the image analyzer also identified a **localized renal abnormality pattern**. This does **not confirm a diagnosis on its own**, but together with your symptoms and history it **strengthens the concern** that there may be a significant renal/urologic or oncologic cause that must be evaluated promptly.\n\n**Most important next steps**\n- **Seek urgent in-person medical care today**\n- Contact your **oncologist or urologist immediately**\n- If you cannot reach them quickly, go to the **emergency department**\n- Tell them clearly: **history of RCC/nephrectomy, visible hematuria, worsening right-sided pain, fever, severe weight loss, fatigue, and concerning CT pipeline result**\n\n**What doctors will likely want to check**\n- **Urinalysis** and urine microscopy\n- **Blood tests**, including kidney function and blood counts\n- **Urgent imaging** such as contrast CT or MRI if appropriate\n- Assessment for **bleeding source, obstruction, infection, recurrence, or progression**\n- Possible **biopsy/tissue confirmation** if imaging shows a suspicious lesion\n\n**When to go to emergency care immediately**\nDo **not wait** if you have any of these now:\n- trouble urinating or very little urine\n- heavy or worsening bleeding in urine\n- severe weakness, faintness, or dizziness\n- worsening fever or chills\n- severe worsening pain\n- shortness of breath or chest pain\n\n**Bottom line**\nThis should be treated as a **potentially serious recurrence or other major kidney/urinary complication until proven otherwise**. Please arrange **same-day urgent medical review**.\n\nI wasn’t able to use the dedicated distillation service because it was unavailable just now, so I distilled it manually here. Are you satisfied with this summary, or do you want me to help you draft a **short urgent message** to send to your oncologist/urologist right now?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0d6bacbc4fba24af0169da6e24b5688191a105b4f692b2c008\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1834,"output":605,"cacheRead":27776,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30215,"cost":{"input":0.0045850000000000005,"output":0.009075,"cacheRead":0.006944,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.020604}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775922710998}}
